verses.1:
A Maskil + 89:1 Maskil is probably a musical or liturgical term; used for Psalms 32, 42, 44–45, 52–55, 74, 78, 88–89, and 142. of Ethan the Ezrahite.
 I will sing of the loving devotion of the LORD forever;
 with my mouth I will proclaim Your faithfulness to all generations.

verses.19:
You once spoke in a vision;
 to Your godly ones You said,
 “I have bestowed help on a warrior;
 I have exalted one chosen from the people.

verses.45:
You have cut short the days of his youth;
 You have covered him with shame.
 Selah
